// name :
"P2803746010" "The Price for Fire"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxHeroArc4Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2200856068" "A Blade of Bronze"
// tDetailString :
"P899638637" "This polished metal blade no longer shines with cosmic energy, as it did when a Pandora entity cut into Doctor Harvan with it. After everything you've been through, in fighting to claim the power from Pandora's Box, you can't help but wonder if all this conflict was the original goal of the Incarnate Zeus. All of this conflict and mayhem may simply be...<br><br><b><color gold>The Price for Fire</color></b><br><br>Your troubles began when Doctor Harvan came to you with a plan to recapture the power released from Pandora's Box. You went to the Freedom Phalanx headquarters, Fort Trident, to retrieve the Antikythera. When you arrived, however, you found the base under attack. Arachnos had overpowered Positron, and had stolen the Antikythera. You fought off the remaining soldiers and spoke with Positron, who expressed his determination in retrieving the artifact.<br><br>Together, you and Positron retrieved the Antikythera, and you brought it back to Doctor Harvan. Harvan led you to his lab, which he claimed had been built based on designs his father had left behind. Harvan activated the device inside, which began to draw in the released energies of Pandora's Box.<br><br>Unfortunately, the Pandora entities that had attacked you earlier arrived as well, and you had to fight off a swarm of golden beings. Just as the device finished its process, Harvan was cut down by an errant attack. You moved to his aid, but Harvan was acting strangely - his speech was muffled by the whirring sounds of broken machinery.<br><br>It was at that moment you realized the truth: James Harvan was an automaton, an artificial creation intended to appear human. Nemesis revealed himself to you, reveling in his plan's success. He then began to empower his automatons with the energy from Pandora's Box, and sent them to destroy you. You escaped intact, but it appears that Nemesis is now in possession of a power of mythical proportions. Who knows what he might have planned..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PositronTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P1957937119" "<color orange>As you approach, Positron struggles to his feet. You can see numerous tears and holes in his armor, where Arachnos managed to punch through his defenses.</color><br><br>{HeroName}... I must say, you have impeccable timing."
// Answer Text :
"P2311487318" "What happened here, Positron?"
// Page Page1 Text :
"P439822765" "Ever since Pandora's Box was opened, the base has been plagued by those creatures that attacked you underneath Zigursky. Doctor Harvan believes that they are drawn to the Antikythera for some reason.<br><br>I can only assume that Arachnos took notice. I was holding them off, but Silver Mantis managed to get behind me while I was occupied by her soldiers. I couldn't keep them at bay and defend against her attacks simultaneously."
// Answer Text :
"P2482818267" "Where's the rest of the Phalanx?"
// Answer Text :
"P607395642" "They took the Antikythera?"
// Page Phalanx Text :
"P3261931791" "They've all been responding to distress calls. Those Pandora creatures have been popping up all over the city, wreaking havoc.<br><br>Thankfully, they generally seek out targets capable of defending themselves - I think they may be drawn to strength - but responses to these attacks has taken up most of the Phalanx's resources."
// Answer Text :
"P1591401023" "What about the Antikythera?"
// Page Stolen Text :
"P221187142" "<color orange>Positron clenches his fists tight.</color><br><br>Arachnos knew exactly what they were looking for, {HeroName}. Given that Mako ambushed you earlier, I'm inclined to believe that Arachnos has been monitoring all of our movements ever since we picked up Doctor Harvan.<br><br>It shouldn't surprise me, really... I consistently underestimate the tenacity of my opponents. It's a flaw I intend to correct immediately."
// Answer Text :
"P2632760181" "Any chance we can pursue them?"
// Page Stolen2 Text :
"P463439127" "<color orange>Positron chuckles softly, making a hollow, metallic sound through his helmet.</color><br><br>I suppose that's the one element of this disaster that I <i>haven't</i> managed to bungle.<br><br><color orange>Positron holds up a small, handheld device. A white light pings repeatedly on the screen.</color><br><br>I planted a tracking device on the Antikythera shortly after it arrived in Fort Trident. Arachnos doesn't appear to have discovered it, so we know where they're taking the artifact."
// Answer Text :
"P2877991471" "Excellent. I'll get it back in no time."
// Page Stolen3 Text :
"P3905127230" "I'm coming with you, {HeroName}. I've been trying my best to manage the Phalanx remotely, to coordinate everyone's efforts in the most efficient way possible... but that's not leadership. I've sat on the sidelines for too long.<br><br>Arachnos attacked me, they attacked the Phalanx, and they stole from us the one hope we have of controlling the chaos of Pandora's Box. I refuse to let that stand. If Arachnos can mobilize a surprise attack when the Phalanx is at its most vulnerable, then I can damn well do the same."
// Answer Text :
"P2423937752" "That's what I like to hear."
// Page TeamTaskIncomplete SayOutLoudText :
"P1082434048" "{HeroName}... I must say, you have impeccable timing."
// Page TeamPage1 SayOutLoudText :
"P2012865266" "Silver Mantis managed to get behind me while I was occupied by her soldiers."
// Page TeamPhalanx SayOutLoudText :
"P1424072084" "The Phalanx has been responding to distress calls. Those Pandora creatures are wreaking havoc in the city."
// Page TeamStolen SayOutLoudText :
"P1738879459" "Arachnos knew exactly what they were looking for. They've probably been monitoring us since we picked up Doctor Harvan."
// Page TeamStolen2 SayOutLoudText :
"P3071672016" "I planted a tracking device on the Antikythera. We know where they're taking it."
// Page TeamStolen3 SayOutLoudText :
"P387279987" "I'm coming with you, {HeroName}. I've sat on the sidelines for too long."
// Page NotTaskOwner Text :
"P2620207394" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress through dialogue."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P856364347" ""
// SendOffString :
"P2528113358" "If we're going to try to contain the freed energy from Pandora's Box, we're going to need to use the one tool known to be capable of altering the Box's power emanations: the Antikythera.<br><br>Currently, I believe, Positron has it held in Fort Trident for safekeeping. We'll need to have it on-hand before we can make any progress towards controlling the power of those creatures."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P68395324" "Retrieve the Antikythera"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3542412469" "{HeroName}, we need the Antikythera before we can proceed. I'm afraid any attempts to corral the energy of Pandora's Box would be futile without it."
// TaskTitle :
"P3087706601" "<color deepskyblue>The Price for Fire</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P766619444" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: The Illusion of Safety</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P411769879" "What's going on here? There are Arachnos agents everywhere!"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P632392217" "Defeat Silver Mantis"
// Script Variable WaypointNames :
"P3168919759" "Silver Mantis"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P2175626791" "Speak with Positron"
// Script Variable WaypointNames :
"P2167503126" "Positron"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - OnEnterObjectiveComplete 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable RescueObjectiveText :
"P4194082598" "Rescue Positron!"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3149781203" "I'm just saying, this was easier than I expected. We should have done this a long time ago!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3907257888" "Oh, SWEET! Two-for-one deal! Let's get {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable CAPTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3621754779" "<t 2><t 0>...Yes, mistress. You're right, of course."
// Script Variable WaveShout :
"P1936714319" "<shout>Stop {HeroName}!"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3609192693" "{HeroName}, it's you."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P892451606" "I die!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4229670543" "You have fended off an Arachnos attack... but not before they could steal the Antikythera!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2021899947" "<color orange>Doctor Harvan pales visibly when you relate the events inside Fort Trident to him.</color><br><br>This is very trying news, {HeroName}. Without the Antikythera, any attempt at containing the energy released by Pandora's Box will be utterly futile. We need to retrieve it as quickly as possible.<br><br>We have time... I doubt Arachnos will be able to decode the Antikythera's readings without at least a few weeks of study. I daresay that they could kidnap the entire mainstream archaeological community and would not gain a single iota of usable knowledge."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PositronTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2009069234" "{HeroName}, I believe it's time. The tracking beacon for the Antikythera has stopped moving somewhere inside the Grandville area of the Rogue Isles.<br><br>I've arranged with Longbow for immediate transportation to the area, but they won't be able to stay for long. We'll need to get inside, retrieve the Antikythera, and leave as quickly as possible. Any delay would give time for the larger bulk of Arachnos's forces to learn of our presence and reinforce their position, which could prove disastrous.<br><br>Are you prepared to depart, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P1801548920" "I'm ready, Positron."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1057976488" "{HeroName}, I'm not sure what to do next. Arachnos controls every island in the Rogue Isles... they could be keeping it anywhere.<br><br><color orange>Harvan shrugs apologetically.</color><br><br>I'm afraid I'm no good in situations like these. What are you planning to do?"
// AcceptString :
"P1620081557" "Positron's tracking the Antikythera's location. We'll have it back in no time."
// SendOffString :
"P1577988953" "<color orange>Harvan's nervous expression fades, and he develops a knowing smile.</color><br><br>I see. Positron always did seem to have things planned out two steps ahead. I daresay that the two of you should be able to make short work of Arachnos's thugs. Give them hell, {HeroName}."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3587694706" "Take Back the Antikythera"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3737037555" "Well? Do you have it?<br><br>...Oh. I'm sorry, {HeroName}, I'm just anxious. Every moment that passes makes it more likely Arachnos will learn how to use the Antikythera, and once they do..."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2045408921" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Men of the Machine</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2594333584" "You've never seen Positron quite like this. He seems... more fired up than usual."
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - OnEnterObjectiveComplete 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P1121873103" "Find the Antikythera"
// Script Variable HERO_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P68527853" "Prepare yourself, {HeroName}. We need to hit Arachnos fast and hard."
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P1127431811" "Hello, {HeroName}."
// BEHAVIORLIST :
"P2562409292" "<t 2>Suit systems failing... I'm running a diagnostic.<t 0>I'm sorry, {HeroName}, but you'll have to handle the fighting from here on."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P4105631639" "Black Scorpion"
// Script Variable BOSS_75HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P972659777" "I'm surprised you found me. Mantis must be getting sloppy."
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3317185925" "<t 1>Still, how'd you get here so quick? It shouldn't have been that- oh, for the love of...<t 0>You planted a bug on it, didn't you? I can't believe this..."
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P927782223" "Hey, BACK OFF! The suit's going critical..."
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P3709510570" "You got... some nerve, {HeroName}..."
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P1419293775" "And stay down!"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2275253406" "Hello there son"
// BEHAVIORLIST :
"P622205182" "<t 3><t 3>Just... figure out how it works! I'm not paying you to scratch your heads. Now, I need to-<t 2><f random:player>{HeroName}! Huh. I guess the jig is up.<t 1>No matter. I've been wanting to beat on something for the past hour. You're just what the doctor ordered!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P313459455" "I don't understand... what power source is it even drawing from?"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3571567476" "Now we die..."
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3108965613" "What the heck are these things?"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P615028242" "They keep coming! Fall back!"
// Script Variable FIGHTER_TWO_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P598937437" "Someone get Black Scorpion up here! We're losing ground!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3351509281" "With Positron's help, you managed to take back the Antikythera."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P707234986" "<color orange>When you produce the Antikythera, Harvan breathes a deep sigh of relief.</color><br><br>Oh, fantastic, {HeroName}! We can get started immediately.<br><br>Come, I have something to show you..."
// RandomFameString :
"P2359444961" "You know, the Freedom Phalanx has really stepped up their game. For the first time since Statesman died, I feel... safe again."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HarvanTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P2179666885" "<color orange>Harvan smiles sheepishly at you.</color><br><br>Welcome to my laboratory, {HeroName}. Impressive, is it not?"
// Answer Text :
"P1398889971" "What is all this, Harvan?"
// Page Harvan1 Text :
"P248701103" "My father had this lab built as a sort of amplifier for the manipulative effects of the Antikythera. If it can establish a firm connection, it magnifies the capabilities of the Antikythera several hundred times, allowing it to draw in any errant energy from Pandora's Box.<br><br>I knew this lab's purpose, but again, I couldn't understand why my father had it built. Everything I knew about Pandora's Box implied that the power would be granted directly to the person that opened it. There would be no need to draw that power from limbo, because I never thought it would manifest in this way.<br><br><color orange>Harvan frowns apprehensively.</color><br><br>Clearly, I missed something in my research. My father knew that the energy would dissipate somehow, but I never saw what it was."
// Answer Text :
"P2114014331" "Do you have any theories?"
// Page Harvan2 Text :
"P2080050278" "<color orange>The subject appears to cause Harvan some level of discomfort.</color><br><br>I'm... not sure, {HeroName}. Perhaps its placement inside Zigursky had altered it in some way, but I find that doubtful. From the evidence you uncovered, no one at Zigursky even knew what Pandora's Box was, much less how it worked.<br><br>The only other explanation is... well. It's probably just me kicking myself for nothing, but...<br><br>The stories about Pandora's Box, and about the gods... there's a sentient force guiding this power, {HeroName}. It blesses mortals with great power, and those mortals go on to live great lives and to do great things. So far, the Box appears to have granted its power to whoever opens it. However...<br><br><color orange>Harvan bites his lip.</color><br><br>It may have found me <i>wanting</i>, somehow. It's possible that the Box simply decided that I wasn't worthy of its power, for whatever reason."
// Answer Text :
"P3738525763" "It's... possible, I suppose."
// Page Harvan3 Text :
"P3983610272" "Regardless, we're here to correct the mistake I made underneath Zigursky. If this device functions as I expect it should, then we'll have possession of all of the power from Pandora's Box, sealed and contained, ready for whatever use you deem fit.<br><br>All you need to do is bring the Antikythera close enough to the device to establish a connection.<br><br>Do be ready for a scuffle, though, {HeroName}. As the energy from Pandora's Box is drawn here, I expect the creatures that attacked us earlier will be arriving as well."
// Answer Text :
"P1048541545" "I can handle them, Harvan. Let's get started."
// Page TeamTaskIncomplete SayOutLoudText :
"P1285322076" "Welcome to my laboratory, {HeroName}. Impressive, is it not?"
// Page TeamHarvan1 SayOutLoudText :
"P320684847" "My father built this lab to amplify the effects of the Antikythera, but I never knew why. Clearly, I missed something in my research."
// Page TeamHarvan2 SayOutLoudText :
"P3064461479" "I'm not sure what happened, {HeroName}. It's possible that the Box simply decided that I wasn't worthy of its power."
// Page TeamHarvan3 SayOutLoudText :
"P396127617" "Bring the Antikythera close enough to the device to establish a connection. Please be ready for a scuffle."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HarvanEndTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P2452567116" "<color orange>Harvan meets your gaze with as much dignity as he can muster. A long, dark gash leads from his shoulder down to his chest. From inside, you can hear faint whirring sounds, like that of a small engine.</color><br><br>{HeroName}. I... I don't quite know what to say..."
// Answer Text :
"P3928434145" "I have no reason to speak with a mindless machine."
// Answer Text :
"P2922305360" "Well-played, Harvan. You had me fooled."
// Answer Text :
"P2766826247" "So, you're one of Nemesis's toys after all."
// Page Mindless Text :
"P578392278" "<color orange>Harvan sputters in protestation.</color><br><br>Mindless machine... but I-<br><br><color orange>A look of profound resignation crosses Harvan's face, and he averts his gaze.</color><br><br>No, no. That... I suppose that is fair. Goodbye, {HeroName}."
// Page Deception Text :
"P3348583166" "<color orange>Harvan takes on an expression of profound resignation.</color><br><br>You and me both, I'm afraid. At my core, I still believe that I am Professor James Harvan, PhD. Memories of my work, of my father...<br><br><color orange>Harvan's brows furrow.</color><br><br>Funny... until now it never really occurred to me that I cannot picture my father's face. I suppose that realization would have been alarming, an hour ago. Now, though, it simply fits. My life, my every experience... it's all a sham, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P2416308887" "So, what are you planning to do now?"
// Page Deception2 Text :
"P1836237498" "<color orange>Harvan chuckles softly. As he does, a soft rattle comes from the opening in his chest.</color><br><br>What <i>indeed</i>, {HeroName}. My every memory and experience have been exposed as a fraud... hah! Even worse than that.<br><br>I <i>know</i> who Nemesis is, {HeroName}. I know his reputation. Plans within plans within <i>plans</i>.<br><br>So, who's to say that my next action isn't simply another part of his grand scheme? What if this <i>very conversation</i> is part of some grand Nemesis Plot?<br><br><color orange>Harvan shakes his head, smiling.</color><br><br>I have <i>no idea</i> what I'm going to do, {HeroName}. I... I need some time to think, before I can make that decision."
// Page Toy Text :
"P3520767253" "<color orange>Harvan barks out a short laugh.</color><br><br>Ha! Quite. A toy! Hahahaha!<br><br><color orange>Harvan's tone devolves into desperation.</color><br><br>I can't properly express my situation to you, {HeroName}. I have <i>no memory</i> of a man named Nemesis, or his plans, or <b><i>anything</b></i> related to him. Until a few minutes ago, I fully believed that I was carrying out my life's work, my <i>legacy</i>. But... none of that really exists, does it? I can't actually have <i>ambitions</i>, can I? It's not possible! It's all just an elaborate hoax, built to deceive! I've got everyone fooled, oh yes I do! Haha!<br><br>You can't understand, {HeroName}. To realize that every facet of your being, not just your actions but your very <i>thoughts</i>, all of it simply a tool for another man to use...<br><br>It is a mountainous revelation, {HeroName}. It crushes me to think on it. And yet... I can do nothing else."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2455321007" "I have a... well, I suppose you would call it a lab. It's something that I inherited when my father passed away. I didn't think I'd ever need to make use of it, but... but circumstances have changed.<br><br><color orange>Doctor Harvan sighs.</color><br><br>I haven't been... completely honest with you, {HeroName}. When I opened Pandora's Box, I expected to inherit the same power as the heroes of Greek myth. All of my research indicated that whomever opens the Box is granted the power of Zeus, and I believed that. I believed that down to the core of my being.<br><br>So, when I learned what my father had built, I didn't understand what it was for."
// AcceptString :
"P3202932006" "...What, exactly, are we talking about, Harvan?"
// SendOffString :
"P635708174" "<color orange>Doctor Harvan appears to be at a loss for words.</color><br><br>Perhaps it would be easier to show you, {HeroName}. The lab isn't far. I think things might be easier to explain once you've seen the lab's equipment."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1552859618" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Parental Ambiguity</color>"

